<task id="081.5" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Refactor RegistrationDataverseService ctor off DemoProvisioningOptions fallback (unblocks task 082)</title>
    <phase>E DemoExpirationService Migration</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Task tags include 'bff-api' + 'deploy'; modifies frozen BFF file at DI-singleton ctor consumed by IHostedService (boot-path); requires pre-deploy Azure App Service config mutation with rollback plan. Fix-drift-at-discovery follow-up to task 082 POML escalation.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Small, focused ctor refactor at known line ranges (RegistrationDataverseService.cs:60-75); pattern already established by sibling tasks 080/081. Boot-path risk is managed by pre-deploy Azure config + rollback snapshot, not by tier escalation. Step 3.5.5b sonnet @ high, matches Phase E siblings.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>080, 081</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, dataverse, deploy, azure-deployment, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Refactor src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs to remove the [Obsolete] fallback branch at ctor lines 60-75 that consumes DemoProvisioningOptions.Environments/DefaultEnvironment. After this refactor, the ctor requires configuration["DATAVERSE_URL"] with no fallback — so the deploy sequence MUST set DATAVERSE_URL on spaarke-bff-dev BEFORE the refactored code is deployed, or /healthz will fail (500.30 at IHost.StartAsync). Follow the pre-deploy sequence in Steps 1-2 STRICTLY. This task unblocks task 082 (deleting the DemoProvisioning__Environments__* Azure config keys).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in BFF DI singleton lifecycle, IHostedService boot dependencies, Azure App Service config precedence, and pre-deploy safety sequences. Follow ADRs strictly (ADR-010 DI minimalism, ADR-028 auth v2).</role>

  <goal>RegistrationDataverseService ctor requires configuration["DATAVERSE_URL"] only (no [Obsolete] fallback); `_options` field + `IOptions&lt;DemoProvisioningOptions&gt;` ctor param removed if truly unused post-refactor; Azure App Service spaarke-bff-dev has DATAVERSE_URL set BEFORE code deploy; BFF /healthz returns 200 after redeploy; task 082 becomes safe to execute. Publish-size delta reported per NFR-01.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 082 POML escalation trigger fired 2026-08-18: pre-verification grep surfaced live production binding to the "orphan" [Obsolete] properties at RegistrationDataverseService.cs:60-75. Tasks 080/081 migrated DemoExpirationService + RegistrationEndpoints but did NOT touch RegistrationDataverseService. Because this class is a DI singleton (RegistrationModule.cs:32) consumed by DemoExpirationService (IHostedService), its ctor runs at IHost.StartAsync(). On spaarke-bff-dev today, DATAVERSE_URL is NOT set — the fallback branch (`_options.Environments[0].DataverseUrl`) is the LIVE source of `_apiUrl`. If task 082 deletes the DemoProvisioning keys with the current code in place, the ctor throws → BFF 500.30 → /healthz down. This task removes the fallback dependency so the config deletion becomes safe.

Per project CLAUDE.md fix-drift-at-discovery principle (established this session, saved as user feedback memory): drift discovered mid-task MUST be fixed properly, not deferred. Path C (author 081.5) chosen over Path A (add DATAVERSE_URL + leave dead fallback code) because Path A leaves the [Obsolete] class wired forever, contradicting FR-33 retirement.

CANONICAL INSIGHT: DataverseEnvironmentService (sibling class) does NOT help here — it also requires DATAVERSE_URL at ctor time for HttpClient BaseAddress. The bootstrap URL is fundamentally a config value, not a Dataverse-lookup value. The proper refactor is "remove the fallback branch entirely, keep the DATAVERSE_URL branch." Do NOT attempt to migrate onto DataverseEnvironmentService — different concerns.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs</file>
      <file role="reference-do-not-modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/RegistrationModule.cs</file>
      <file role="reference-do-not-modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/DemoProvisioningOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="reference-do-not-modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/DataverseEnvironmentService.cs (parallel bootstrap pattern)</file>
      <file role="escalation-context">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-082-deviations.md</file>
      <file role="rollback-snapshot">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/phase-e-config-snapshot.json</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="080" status="✅">DemoExpirationService migration (commit 5fdd1d9ea)</dependency>
      <dependency task="081" status="✅">RegistrationEndpoints migration (commit 0b8ca53ba)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <blocks>
      <blocked-task id="082">Delete DemoProvisioning__Environments__* + __DefaultEnvironment Azure config keys</blocked-task>
    </blocks>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="fix-drift-at-discovery">SCOPE: Complete FR-33 [Obsolete] retirement properly — remove the fallback code AND deploy so it takes effect. Do NOT ship a "half-fix" that leaves the fallback branch in production while Azure config masks the drift.</constraint>
    <constraint source="deploy-safety">SCOPE: Azure config mutation MUST precede code deploy. NEVER deploy the refactored code with DATAVERSE_URL unset — boot crash at IHost.StartAsync. Order: (1) `az webapp config appsettings set` DATAVERSE_URL, (2) verify current unmodified BFF /healthz still 200 (should be — old code has fallback), (3) commit + push refactor, (4) publish + deploy, (5) verify /healthz again.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE: BFF-touching task — load .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md; /conflict-check before PR; publish-size delta reported per NFR-01; update tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ if RegistrationDataverseService has ctor tests that need the DemoProvisioningOptions param removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">SCOPE: Post-refactor, ctor MUST fail fast at boot on missing DATAVERSE_URL (throw InvalidOperationException). Current behavior already throws when both sources empty — refactor tightens to "DATAVERSE_URL required" only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE: DI minimalism — do NOT introduce new interfaces or wrapper classes. Just remove the fallback branch + drop unused ctor param.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">SCOPE: Auth path unchanged — TokenCredential injection stays; refactor only touches the URL resolution.</constraint>
    <constraint source="god-class-ratchet">SCOPE: RegistrationDataverseService is a large existing file — this refactor REDUCES LOC (removes ~15 lines including `#pragma` block, fallback branch, `_options` field, ctor param). Ratchet allows shrinkage.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: RegistrationDataverseService's public API + all method signatures stay identical. This is a pure internal ctor refactor.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: DemoProvisioningOptions class stays (other 7 files still consume other properties — AccountDomain, Licenses, etc.). Only remove the [Obsolete] Environments/DefaultEnvironment consumers within RegistrationDataverseService.</constraint>
    <constraint source="testing">SCOPE: If tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ contains constructor tests for RegistrationDataverseService that reference IOptions&lt;DemoProvisioningOptions&gt;, update them to drop the removed param. Do NOT skip — TEST-MODIFYING override triggers unconditional code-review + adr-check per root §8.</constraint>
    <constraint source="deploy-verification">SCOPE: /healthz MUST return 200 AFTER refactored code is deployed. If it fails, execute the rollback plan in Step 9 IMMEDIATELY.</constraint>
  </constraints>

