  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, TEST-MODIFYING override if tests exist). Load .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md + .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md + projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-082-deviations.md.</step>

    <step order="1" name="Pre-check current dev state (baseline)">Verify unmodified BFF is currently healthy: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" https://spaarke-bff-dev.azurewebsites.net/healthz` → MUST return 200. If NOT 200, STOP and escalate (something else is broken, not this task's problem). Record baseline in task notes.</step>

    <step order="2" name="Set DATAVERSE_URL on spaarke-bff-dev (PRE-DEPLOY GATE — must precede code deploy)">Run: `az webapp config appsettings set --resource-group rg-spaarke-dev --name spaarke-bff-dev --settings DATAVERSE_URL=https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com` — this triggers a slot restart. Wait ~30s. Re-verify /healthz returns 200 (proves old-code path still works with both sources present). CHECK if there are staging slots via `az webapp deployment slot list --resource-group rg-spaarke-dev --name spaarke-bff-dev`; if slots exist, apply the same setting to ALL slots (T5 slot-parity invariant). Record in task notes.</step>

    <step order="3" name="Refactor RegistrationDataverseService.cs">Edit src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs:
      (a) Line 32: DELETE `private readonly DemoProvisioningOptions _options;` field
      (b) Line 46-52: In ctor signature, REMOVE `IOptions&lt;DemoProvisioningOptions&gt; options,` parameter
      (c) Line 55: DELETE `_options = options.Value;`
      (d) Lines 60-75: REPLACE the entire block with:
```csharp
        // Admin Dataverse URL: required config (no fallback per FR-33 retirement).
        var dataverseUrl = configuration["DATAVERSE_URL"];
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(dataverseUrl))
        {
            throw new InvalidOperationException(
                "RegistrationDataverseService requires DATAVERSE_URL configuration.");
        }
```
      (e) Verify no other references to `_options` or `DemoProvisioningOptions` remain in this file (grep-verify).
      (f) Verify `using Microsoft.Extensions.Options;` can be removed if IOptions is no longer used in this file.</step>

    <step order="4" name="Verify DI still resolves">Read src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/RegistrationModule.cs — confirm `services.AddSingleton&lt;RegistrationDataverseService&gt;();` at line 32 does NOT need changes (DI resolves ctor params by type; removing a param is transparent to registration). Do NOT modify RegistrationModule.cs unless a compile error forces you to.</step>

    <step order="5" name="Test updates">Grep tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ for `new RegistrationDataverseService(` and `IOptions&lt;DemoProvisioningOptions&gt;` — if constructor tests exist that pass the removed param, update them to drop it. Follow the RecordMatchServiceTests drift-3 pattern (Wave 4E) as reference for minimal test surgery.</step>

    <step order="6" name="Build + Test">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — 0 errors, warnings unchanged or reduced (this refactor may reduce the [Obsolete] warning count in the BFF from ~4 to 0 if the ctor was the last consumer of `.Environments`/`.DefaultEnvironment` — verify via `dotnet build 2&gt;&amp;1 | grep -i CS0618`). Run `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` — all pass. Run `dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/` — all pass (no new god-class ratchet trip; this shrinks the file).</step>

    <step order="7" name="Publish + Deploy">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`. Report compressed size + delta vs current baseline (44.96 MB incl. PDBs per CLAUDE.md §10 baseline). Deploy to spaarke-bff-dev via existing deploy mechanism (script or `az webapp deploy` — check scripts/Deploy-Release.ps1 for the canonical command; do NOT invent a new deploy path).</step>

    <step order="8" name="Verify /healthz post-deploy">Wait for deploy to complete + slot restart (~1-2 min). Verify: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" https://spaarke-bff-dev.azurewebsites.net/healthz` → MUST return 200. Also verify: BFF logs for `RegistrationDataverseService targeting Dataverse at https://spaarkedev1.crm.dynamics.com/api/data/v9.2` on startup (proves DATAVERSE_URL branch executed, not throw-branch). If /healthz != 200, execute Step 9 IMMEDIATELY.</step>

    <step order="9" name="Rollback plan (execute ONLY if Step 8 fails)">If /healthz returns non-200 after Step 8:
      (a) Revert code: `git revert HEAD --no-edit` then push
      (b) Redeploy old code: same deploy command as Step 7
      (c) Verify /healthz recovers to 200
      (d) DO NOT remove DATAVERSE_URL from App Service (harmless if unused; keeps it available for retry)
      (e) File deviations note in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/task-081.5-rollback.md with root cause
      (f) Escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT retry blindly</step>

    <step order="10" name="CVE + publish-size compliance">`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — zero HIGH. Report publish size in task notes: absolute (MB) + delta vs prior baseline. If delta &gt; +5 MB, add explicit justification per CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4 (unlikely — this refactor should be neutral or slightly negative).</step>

    <step order="11" name="TASK-INDEX + current-task.md update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: add new row 081.5 between 081 and 082, status ✅. Update task 082 row's deps from "080, 081 + deploy" to "080, 081, 081.5 + deploy". Update current-task.md to reflect 081.5 completion + task 082 now unblocked.</step>

    <step order="12" name="Commit">Single commit: `refactor(bff-registration): remove [Obsolete] DemoProvisioningOptions fallback in RegistrationDataverseService (task 081.5)`. Body: cite task-082-deviations.md as root cause; note pre-deploy Azure config gate (DATAVERSE_URL set on dev) in commit body per fix-drift-at-discovery discipline; report publish-size delta + /healthz verification.</step>
  </steps>

